[{:db/id 17592186229191 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-2a7ae8c6-87fd-5aaa-b1ca-f181d86f7e93" "question-6c38c2df-a1c4-591d-95c2-93cd739693be" "question-5b2ce271-5eac-5d80-b8db-22d863d22bcd"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-2a7ae8c6-87fd-5aaa-b1ca-f181d86f7e93" :question/id #uuid "2a7ae8c6-87fd-5aaa-b1ca-f181d86f7e93" :question/math-academy-id "q-334936" :question/problem "Given that $P(t)={\\int }_{-2}^{0}(x-3t)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x,$ calculate ${P}^{′}(t)$ for $t\\in R$ by differentiating under the integral sign.\n\n${P}^{′}(t)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Suppose $f(x,t)$ is continuous on $R=[a,b]\\times [c,d]$ and $\\frac{∂f}{∂t}$ exists and is continuous on $R.$ Then, the function\n\n$$\nF(t)={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x,t)\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nis differentiable on $(c,d),$ and\n\n$$\n{F}^{′}(t)=\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x,t)\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\frac{∂f}{∂t}(x,t)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nThis is known as *differentiating under the integral sign.*\n\nWe wish to compute ${P}^{′}(t),$ where\n\n$$\nP(t)={\\int }_{-2}^{0}(x-3t)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating under the integral sign, we get\n\n$$\n{P}^{′}(t)={\\int }_{-2}^{0}\\frac{∂}{∂t}[(x-3t)^{2}]\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nNext, let's compute the partial derivative with respect to $t$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂t}[(x-3t)^{2}] & =2(x-3t)\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂t}(x-3t) \\\\  & =2(x-3t)\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & =-6(x-3t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this back into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}^{′}(t) & ={\\int }_{-2}^{0}-6(x-3t)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-6{\\int }_{-2}^{0}(x-3t)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, let's evaluate the remaining integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-2}^{0}(x-3t)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-2}^{0}x\\,\\text{d}x-{\\int }_{-2}^{0}3t\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}{|}_{-2}^{0}-3tx{|}_{-2}^{0} \\\\  & =-2-6t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}^{′}(t) & =-6(-2-6t) \\\\  & =12(3t+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-831d751e-c629-5b32-9f44-368844ac1a78"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-831d751e-c629-5b32-9f44-368844ac1a78" :answer-field/id #uuid "831d751e-c629-5b32-9f44-368844ac1a78" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-ba4b594e-6e46-5106-afac-33e43b94aed5" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ba4b594e-6e46-5106-afac-33e43b94aed5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ba4b594e-6e46-5106-afac-33e43b94aed5" :answer/id #uuid "ba4b594e-6e46-5106-afac-33e43b94aed5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "36t+12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-6c38c2df-a1c4-591d-95c2-93cd739693be" :question/id #uuid "6c38c2df-a1c4-591d-95c2-93cd739693be" :question/math-academy-id "q-334973" :question/problem "Given that $P(t)={\\int }_{-1}^{1}(x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t))^{2}\\,\\text{d}x,$ calculate ${P}^{′}(t)$ for $t\\in R$ by differentiating under the integral sign.\n\n${P}^{′}(t)=4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)\\,$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Suppose $f(x,t)$ is continuous on $R=[a,b]\\times [c,d]$ and $\\frac{∂f}{∂t}$ exists and is continuous on $R.$ Then, the function\n\n$$\nF(t)={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x,t)\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nis differentiable on $(c,d),$ and\n\n$$\n{F}^{′}(t)=\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x,t)\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\frac{∂f}{∂t}(x,t)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nThis is known as *differentiating under the integral sign.*\n\nWe wish to compute ${P}^{′}(t),$ where\n\n$$\nP(t)={\\int }_{-1}^{1}(x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t))^{2}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating under the integral sign, we get\n\n$$\n{P}^{′}(t)={\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\frac{∂}{∂t}[(x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t))^{2}]\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nNext, let's compute the partial derivative with respect to $t$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂t}[(x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t))^{2}] & =2(x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t))\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂t}(x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)) \\\\  & =2(x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t))\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(t) \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)(x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this back into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}^{′}(t) & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)(x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t))\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t){\\int }_{-1}^{1}(x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t))\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, let's evaluate the remaining integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}(x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t))\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}x\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}{|}_{-1}^{1}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)\\cdot x{|}_{-1}^{1} \\\\  & =0+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{P}^{′}(t)=4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t).\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-a8e8dcc5-5048-58a4-a50f-532f28ef34ce"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-a8e8dcc5-5048-58a4-a50f-532f28ef34ce" :answer-field/id #uuid "a8e8dcc5-5048-58a4-a50f-532f28ef34ce" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-c3937af2-b650-5eaa-a987-e97fd137f52f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c3937af2-b650-5eaa-a987-e97fd137f52f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c3937af2-b650-5eaa-a987-e97fd137f52f" :answer/id #uuid "c3937af2-b650-5eaa-a987-e97fd137f52f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\cos(t)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186311550 :question/problem "For which of the following functions is it valid to differentiate under the integral sign?\n\nI. ${F}_{1}(t)={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{x+t}\\,\\text{d}x,\\,t>0$\n\nII. ${F}_{2}(t)={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{xt}{{x}^{2}+{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x,\\,t>0$\n\nIII. ${F}_{3}(t)={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{x-t}\\,\\text{d}x,\\,t>1$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186311552 :question/problem "For which of the following functions is it valid to differentiate under the integral sign?\n\nI. ${F}_{1}(t)={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{{t}^{2}}{{x}^{2}+{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x,\\,t>0$\n\nII. ${F}_{2}(t)={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{|x-t|}}\\,\\text{d}x,\\,t\\in (0,1)$\n\nIII. ${F}_{3}(t)={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+{t}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x,\\,t>0$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-5b2ce271-5eac-5d80-b8db-22d863d22bcd" :question/id #uuid "5b2ce271-5eac-5d80-b8db-22d863d22bcd" :question/math-academy-id "q-352887" :question/problem "Given that $K(t)={\\int }_{0}^{4}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)-3x)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x,$ calculate ${K}^{′}(t)$ for $t\\in R$ by differentiating under the integral sign.\n\n${K}^{′}(t)=8\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)(\\,$\n{{field-1}}$)$" :question/worked-solution "Suppose $f(x,t)$ is continuous on $R=[a,b]\\times [c,d]$ and $\\frac{∂f}{∂t}$ exists and is continuous on $R.$ Then, the function\n\n$$\nF(t)={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x,t)\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nis differentiable on $(c,d),$ and\n\n$$\n{F}^{′}(t)=\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x,t)\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\frac{∂f}{∂t}(x,t)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nThis is known as differentiating under the integral sign.\n\nWe wish to compute ${K}^{′}(t),$ where\n\n$$\nK(t)={\\int }_{0}^{4}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)-3x)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating under the integral sign, we get\n\n$$\n{K}^{′}(t)={\\int }_{0}^{4}\\frac{∂}{∂t}[(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)-3x)^{2}]\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nNext, let's compute the partial derivative with respect to $t$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂t}[(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)-3x)^{2}] & =2(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)-3x)\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)-3x) \\\\  & =2(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)-3x)\\cdot (\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)) \\\\  & =2(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)-3x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this back into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{K}^{′}(t) & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}2(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)-3x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t){\\int }_{0}^{4}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)-3x)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, let's evaluate the remaining integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{4}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)-3x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)\\,\\text{d}x-{\\int }_{0}^{4}3x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t))\\,x{|}_{0}^{4}-\\frac{3}{2}{x}^{2}{|}_{0}^{4} \\\\  & =4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)-24\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{K}^{′}(t) & =2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)\\cdot (4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)-24) \\\\  & =8\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)-6).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-d4f3822a-92a6-5439-9a5d-bf0f8c9a91bb"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-d4f3822a-92a6-5439-9a5d-bf0f8c9a91bb" :answer-field/id #uuid "d4f3822a-92a6-5439-9a5d-bf0f8c9a91bb" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-49bfc920-4798-5ac8-829c-10c6425543fd" :answer-field/choices ["answer-49bfc920-4798-5ac8-829c-10c6425543fd"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-49bfc920-4798-5ac8-829c-10c6425543fd" :answer/id #uuid "49bfc920-4798-5ac8-829c-10c6425543fd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sin(t)-6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-cf6c0bba-9840-5282-9c1e-6b17cae9759d" :activity/id #uuid "cf6c0bba-9840-5282-9c1e-6b17cae9759d" :activity/title "Differentiating Under the Integral Sign" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186048817 :activity/course 17592186046659 :activity/steps ["step-452238fc-0a14-5395-9d29-80eea1eaebf3" "step-0b5c3e8c-b479-5b7c-995d-1b489fe05efc" "step-c87a8b02-417c-5ed5-80b6-82dec3b064cd" "step-86e12b8a-080a-53fd-a5ee-62fcb2d5ac6b" 